{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"One unrelated test failed in this ticket's full-suite run and did NOT reproduce. Recording it as an open question rather than a diagnosis.\n\nThe failure: tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_ref_coherence.py::test_attested_claim_gate_ignores_unrelated_committed_change — 'rebar._errors.RebarError: rebar create failed (exit 1): Error: git commit f…' (truncated; the suite ran under -q so the traceback is lost). 1 failed, 12859 passed.\n\nWhat I checked:\n- Isolated re-run: passed in 64s.\n- Reproduction sweep: three consecutive runs of tests/interfaces/lifecycle/ at -n 3 --dist worksteal, 448 tests each, ALL PASSED (169s, 162s, 265s). Not reproduced in ~1344 test executions.\n- My first hypothesis was store-lock contention from the concurrent session that held the tracker flock for 100s+ stretches all afternoon. Reading the test REFUTES that: _repo() builds a repo under tmp_path and monkeypatches REBAR_ROOT to it, so it never touches the shared tracker. I discarded the hypothesis rather than reporting it.\n\nWhat I did NOT conclude: a root cause. The git-commit failure inside an isolated temp repo has no explanation I can support with evidence, and the traceback that would have supplied one was discarded by -q.\n\nWhy it is not attributable to this change: this diff is CONTRIBUTING.md, AGENTS.md, src/rebar/_guides/passing-code-review.md, and one new test module. None is reachable from attest.claim_gate_check or the store write path.\n\nLeft as an open question, not filed as a bug: a single unreproduced failure with no traceback does not meet the bar for a bug ticket that someone else would have to act on, and filing it would be indistinguishable from noise. If it recurs on CI, the run log will have the traceback under CI's own verbosity and it should be filed then, with this comment as the first datapoint."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786653850633251001,"uuid":"60b30d70-aeff-442a-af1a-7b9df124f9d0"}